<Base title="About" path="/about">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lede">I am Lin Zhu, a staff QA engineer. I have spent about twenty years in software testing, and the last few building the things that make a QA team faster: test tooling, shared services, and lately AI agents that plan and write tests with a human at every gate.</p>
  <p>This site is a personal notebook. I write about what changes for testers when development gets AI, how to keep an LLM agent safe on systems many people share, and the small engineering habits that make automation trustworthy. Everything here is my own view, written in general terms — no employer specifics.</p>
  <p>Find me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/linzhu1989/">LinkedIn</a>. Posts are also mirrored on dev.to.</p>
</Base>
